   "description": "Follows ivrit.ai's Hebrew evaluation normalizer (github.com/ivrit-ai/asr-training, evaluate_model.py, HebrewTextNormalizer): remove bidirectional and zero-width marks, remove niqqud, drop the quote characters written for geresh and gershayim so acronyms compare as one word, then Whisper's BasicTextNormalizer (case folding, punctuation and symbols to spaces, whitespace collapsed). Cadence departs in two places: the Hebrew geresh (U+05F3) and gershayim (U+05F4) are joined like their ASCII stand-ins (ivrit.ai turns them into spaces, so צה״ל and צה\"ל scored differently), the typographic quotes word processors put in their place (U+2018, U+2019, U+201C, U+201D) are joined too, and the maqaf (U+05BE) splits words explicitly. Combining marks (niqqud U+05B0–U+05C7 and cantillation U+0591–U+05AF) are removed after canonical decomposition. Numbers are compared as written until the language pack's inverse normalisation arrives (phase 4)."
  },
